outcome:
docs/features/review-freeze-verification.md describes the reviewer input-identity contract that w-228b introduces, and docs/features/agent-delegation-sessions.md links to it. The description covers:
- the admitted manifest at .git/termal-review-input-<id>-<n>.json;
- the rule that the last check must be Verified;
- the identity-* refusal codes and the 429 publication and observation in-flight refusals;
- the inputIdentity envelope field;
- the boot fail-closed drift;
- what happens when the reviewer's cwd is not a Git worktree root, is not Git, or has configured filters: it can then submit only status failed without findings.
The coordinator confirms that the non-root behaviour is the intended scope, or the change admits at the enclosing worktree root instead.
